[s0l0!-header][h1]while Loops[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

A [b]loop [/b]statement allows to repeatedly execute a statement or group of statements.

A [b]while [/b]loop statement repeatedly executes a target statement as long as a given condition is true.

[s0l0!-header][b]Example:[/b][/s0l0!-header][code format="java" codeId="738"]int x = 3;

[b]while[/b](x > 0) {
   System.out.println(x);
   x--;
}
[/code]
The [b]while [/b]loops check for the condition x > 0. If it evaluates to true, it executes the statements within its body. Then it checks for the statement again and repeats.
[note]Notice the statement x--. This decrements x each time the loop runs, and makes the loop stop when x reaches 0. 
Without the statement, the loop would run forever.[/note]

