When the expression is tested and the result is false, the loop body is skipped and the first statement after the while loop is executed.
[s0l0!-header][b]Example:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [code format="java" codeId="739"]int x = 6;

[b]while[/b]( x < 10 )
{
  System.out.println(x);
  x++;
}
System.out.println("Loop ended");

/*
6
7
8
9
Loop ended
*/[/code]
[note]Notice that the last print method is out of the while scope.[/note]
